    "math_academy_id": "q-131521",
    "knowledge_point_id": "607e0800-870c-5271-9220-0489d9c5b891",
    "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval",
    "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-1.99<Z<-0.99).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr> \n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-2.0\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0192\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0188\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0183\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.9\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0244\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0239\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0233\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.8\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0307\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0301\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.0294\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-1.0\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1423\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1401\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1379\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.9\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1660\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1635\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1611\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.8\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1922\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1894\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.1867\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
    "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.99<Z<-0.99).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/8dc66c8ceed4366688dc040104eaece3d251ecb9f72d9aae0827ead3fe933570.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.99<Z<-0.99) & =P(Z<-0.99)-P(Z\\le -1.99) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.99)-P(Z\\le -1.99) \\\\  & =Φ(-0.99)-Φ(-1.99).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.99) & =0.0233 \\\\ Φ(-0.99) & =0.1611\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.99<Z<-0.99) & =Φ(-0.99)-Φ(-1.99) \\\\  & =0.1611-0.0233 \\\\  & =0.1378.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
